cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "BLASTHub: bulk nucleotide sequence search on managed NCBI BLAST+ infrastructure"
message: "If you use this software in work you publish, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  # Mononym: recorded with given-names only. CFF 1.2.0 allows a person with a
  # single name; adding a family-names field would invent a surname.
  - given-names: Vipin
    email: sainivipin839@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-2924-7095"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vipin839/superblast"
url: "https://superblast.app"
abstract: >-
  BLASTHub is a web application for bulk nucleotide sequence search. It executes
  genuine NCBI BLAST+ blastn searches against pre-indexed reference databases on
  managed cloud infrastructure and returns native JSON-15 output parsed into an
  interactive hit table with per-HSP pairwise alignments. Reference databases are
  pinned to specific NCBI assembly accessions with recorded checksums, and the
  build verifies each database with blastdbcmd before shipping. Results can be
  exported as a multi-sheet Excel workbook, a PDF report, or raw JSON and CSV.
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - BLAST
  - sequence alignment
  - nucleotide
  - genomics
  - web application
license: MIT
version: 2.1.2
date-released: "2026-09-10"

